      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    face_value = 1000\n    annual_coupon = 50\n    term_years = 5\n    yield_to_maturity = 0.04\n\n    cash_flows = [annual_coupon] * (term_years - 1)\n    cash_flows.append(annual_coupon + face_value)\n\n    # Calculate the bond price and present-value-weighted cash flows\n    present_values = [\n        cash_flow / ((1 + yield_to_maturity) ** year)\n        for year, cash_flow in enumerate(cash_flows, start=1)\n    ]\n    bond_price = sum(present_values)\n\n    weighted_present_value = sum(\n        year * present_value\n        for year, present_value in enumerate(present_values, start=1)\n    )\n\n    # Calculate Macaulay duration\n    macaulay_duration = weighted_present_value / bond_price\n\n    # Return the answer rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(macaulay_duration, 2)\n```",
